    int[] a=readings; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {PriorityQueue<Integer>heap=new PriorityQueue<>();for(int x:a)heap.add(x);while(!heap.isEmpty())out.add(heap.remove());}
    int answer=0;for(int x:out)if(x%2==0)answer++;return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Insert all readings into a binary min-heap and repeatedly remove the smallest. Produce that removal sequence, preserving duplicates.

Return how many values in the derived sequence are even, including 0 and negative even values.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n log n); space O(n).

